                "xpath": "/html[1]/body[1]/div[4]/div[2]/div[1]/div[12]/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]",
                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew Letter Nun Fourteen Letter Of Hebrew Alphabet Meaning ...](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-59cd66f7699e:4)\nNun Sofit (**ן** ) is the special final form of the fourteenth Hebrew letter, Nun (**נ**).[[1]](https://www.facebook.com/100068612731591/posts/how-to-write-the-hebrew-letter-nun-in-blockscriptnun-%D7%A0-final-nun-%D7%9F-alphabetical-/851145567182527/)[[2]](https://kriakala.com/hebrew-letter-nun)\n\n### Key Facts\n\n- **When it is used:** It replaces the standard Nun whenever the letter appears at the very end of a word.[[1]](https://kriakala.com/hebrew-letter-nun)\n- **Sound:** It makes the \"n\" sound (as in \"noon\").[[1]](https://www.facebook.com/100068612731591/posts/how-to-write-the-hebrew-letter-nun-in-blockscriptnun-%D7%A0-final-nun-%D7%9F-alphabetical-/851145567182527/)\n- **Shape:** Unlike the regular curved or bent Nun, Nun Sofit is a straight vertical line that extends downward below the baseline.[[1]](https://www.mayimachronim.com/secrets-of-the-five-special-sofit-letters/)[[2]](https://kriakala.com/hebrew-letter-nun)\n- **Numerical Value:** It equals **50** (or **700** in rare gematria systems when used as a final form).[[1]](https://www.equipgodspeople.com/bible-study-tools/lexicons-word-study/old-testament-hebrew/nun/)\n- **Part of Mantzepach:** It belongs to the group of five Hebrew letters with special end-of-word forms known as *Mantzepach* (**מנצפ״ך** — Kaf, Mem, Nun, Pe, and Tsadi).[[1]](https://www.mayimachronim.com/secrets-of-the-five-special-sofit-letters/)[[2]](https://www.thelivingword.org.au/grand-design/session32.php)\n\nYou can practice reading and recognizing letters with visual guides on [Cartoon Hebrew](https://www.cartoonhebrew.com/nun-sofit) or learn more about letter structures at [Hebrew4Christians](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Nun/nun.html).[[1]](https://www.cartoonhebrew.com/nun-sofit)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Nun/nun.html)Would you like to see **examples of Hebrew words** that use Nun Sofit, or learn about **other Sofit letters**?",
